  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 20.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="302" ed="#liebermann"/>And eac ah hlaforda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.1"/> gehwylc þæs formycle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.2"/> þearfe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he his men rihtlice healde.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="302" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ eac ah laforda gehwylc ðæs formyccle ðearfe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he his men rihtlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="302" ed="#liebermann"/>And eac ah hlaforda gehwylc þæs formicele þearfe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he his menn rihtlice heolde.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.1-3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="303" ed="#liebermann"/>Et unicuique domino magnum opus est, ut hominem suum recte deducat.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.1-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="303" ed="#liebermann"/>Sic et dominum quemque suos homines recte seruare oportet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="170" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ eac ah laforda gehwylc ðæs formyccle ðearfe þæt he his men rihtlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="248" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And eac ah hlaforda gehwylc þæs formycle þearfe þæt he his men rihtlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="303" ed="#liebermann"/>Und auch jeder der Herren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_20-2.lnote.de.1"/> hat dazu gar<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_20-2.lnote.de.2"/> starke Verpflichtung, dass er seine Untergebenen rechtlich halte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And also every lord has very great need to treat his men rightly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_20-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="171" ed="#robertson"/>And likewise it is the great<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_20-2.robnote.n.2"/> duty of every lord to treat his men justly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="462" ed="#whitelock"/>And also every lord has very great benefit from treating his men justly.<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_20-2.whinote.n.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="249" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And likewise the principal obligation of every lord is to treat his people justly.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 303, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rd <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rd Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-micele <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-micele Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heolde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heolde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">303</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">edu. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">edu. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20-2.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_20-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">beo hlaforda gehwylc milde his mannum ond hy næfre ne swence on unriht to swyðe</hi>; <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 74. Zu Milde gegen die Leute mahnt geistlich den Herrn Episc. 10, <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. I 478; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Gefolge 14a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">beo hlaforda gehwylc milde his mannum ond hy næfre ne swence on unriht to swyðe</hi>; <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 74. Episc. 10, <hi rend="italic">above</hi> I 478, exhorts the lord, on religious grounds, to mildness towards his people; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Gefolge 14a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_20-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Komponiert wie <hi rend="italic">formanig</hi> ‘sehr viele’ (Toller), <hi rend="italic">foroft</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Compounded like <hi rend="italic">formanig</hi> ‘very many’ (Toller), <hi rend="italic">foroft</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>)</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_20-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann compares this with <hi rend="italic">Episcopus</hi>, 10 (see <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>. p. 478).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_20-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">formanig</hi>, <hi rend="italic">foroft</hi>, BT., p. 315.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="ICn_20-2.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">462</biblScope></bibl><label>justly</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">I omit the rest of this code</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
